---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';
---
<Layout title="Technical Support & Remote Assistance | Syntax" description="Get technical help from Syntax. Open the AlgaPSA client portal to submit and track support tickets, or request coordinated remote assistance through Level.">
  <section class="page-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="square"></span> CLIENT SUPPORT</p>
    <h1>Technical support.<br />Get back to work<span class="accent">.</span></h1>
    <div class="page-hero-bottom">
      <p>A technology hiccup shouldn’t derail your day.<br class="desktop-break" /> Start here for help with your business technology.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">New project? Let’s talk <Icon name="arrow" size={19} /></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="help-grid container" aria-label="Support options">
    <article class="help-card help-card-remote" aria-labelledby="remote-heading">
      <div class="card-top"><Icon name="it" size={30} /><span class="eyebrow">01 / REMOTE ASSISTANCE</span></div>
      <h2 id="remote-heading">A helping hand.<br />Wherever you work.</h2>
      <p>Syntax uses Level to provide remote assistance on enrolled devices. Send a request first so we can arrange a session and confirm any setup you need.</p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Tell us which device needs help and what’s happening.</li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Keep the device powered on and connected to the internet.</li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />We coordinate with you before starting remote assistance.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="help-card-action">
        <a class="button button-light" href="/contact/?plan=Remote%20assistance">Request remote assistance <Icon name="arrow" size={18} /></a>
        <p class="help-caption">Opens our contact form. Sending a request does not start a remote session or create an AlgaPSA ticket. Existing clients can also request assistance through the <a href={business.clientPortalUrl}>client portal</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="help-card" aria-labelledby="portal-heading">
      <div class="card-top"><Icon name="strategy" size={30} /><span class="help-status">CLIENT PORTAL</span></div>
      <h2 id="portal-heading">Your support.<br />All in one place.</h2>
      <p>Our AlgaPSA client portal gives existing clients a place to submit support tickets and follow up on their requests. Sign in with your client account to get started.</p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Submit a support ticket.</li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Follow updates and reply to your requests.</li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Keep your support conversations together.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="help-card-action">
        <a class="button button-outline" href={business.clientPortalUrl} aria-describedby="portal-status">Open client portal <Icon name="arrow" size={18} /></a>
        <p class="help-caption" id="portal-status">Need access or help signing in? <a href="/contact/">Contact Syntax</a>. Our contact form sends an email request, not an AlgaPSA ticket.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="remote-steps-heading">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="square"></span> BEFORE WE CONNECT</p><h2 id="remote-steps-heading">Clear steps.<br />No surprise connections.</h2></div>
      <p>Remote assistance is coordinated with Syntax. There’s no public session code or automatic connection on this page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <article><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Tell us what’s wrong.</h3><p>Include your company, the affected device or application, any error message, and how the issue affects your work. Don’t include passwords or sensitive data.</p></article>
      <article><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>We arrange the next step.</h3><p>We’ll follow up about your request. If your device isn’t enrolled in Level, we’ll discuss setup before sending installation instructions directly.</p></article>
      <article><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Connect with confidence.</h3><p>Confirm you’re speaking with Syntax before installing software or granting permissions. Keep your device online and review any approval prompt when we connect.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section container" aria-labelledby="support-faq-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="square"></span> A LITTLE MORE CLARITY</p><h2 id="support-faq-heading">Good to know.</h2></div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details><summary>Can I start a remote session from this page?<Icon name="plus" size={20} /></summary><p>No. The remote assistance button opens a request form. A Syntax technician starts the session from Level after coordinating with you; your device needs the Level agent installed and online.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need to download anything?<Icon name="plus" size={20} /></summary><p>If your device is already enrolled, you don’t need a new download from this page. If setup is needed, Syntax will provide instructions directly. We do not publish installers or ask you to run installation commands here.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Where can I check my ticket status?<Icon name="plus" size={20} /></summary><p>Sign in to our <a href={business.clientPortalUrl}>AlgaPSA client portal</a> to view your support tickets, follow updates, and reply. If you need account access, contact Syntax. Requests sent through our website contact form are email inquiries and do not create portal tickets.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="help-service-note container" aria-label="Support availability">
    <span class="square"></span>
    <p>Support availability and response times follow your service agreement. Sending a request does not guarantee an immediate response or 24/7 coverage.</p>
  </aside>
</Layout>
